Ideogram just released their latest and best v4 image model open weights. It is state of the art and open weights go well together.

The model can be downloaded, fine-tuned on your own data, and run on your hardware. It is available on every Ideogram plan and the API today.

@ideogram_ai: "Introducing Ideogram 4.0: the best open image model in the world. Think it. Make it. Own it."

Here's how to use Claude Code with GLM-5.2 via @huggingface Inference Providers: create a token with call permissions, set the environment variables, and then it works. The post includes a visual guide.

@victormustar emphasizes that open source must win. GLM-5.2 is free when used with Hugging Face Inference Providers, and for the next 6 hours, the cost is covered for several providers including Zai, Together AI, Novita, Fireworks, and DeepInfra. Setting it up with Pi, opencode, Codex, Claude Code, or any coding agent demonstrates how open source AI has caught up to proprietary options.

Hugging Face is dedicated to advancing and democratizing AI through open source and open science, supporting the community building the future.

