A new foundation model that reads and generates DNA sequences was just released on Hugging Face. Feel free to test the model's capabilities on the demo space.

@gsbenegas shares MarinDNA, a 1B gLM that rivals Evo 2 40B on variant effect prediction while being 2,330 times faster. They built it around a standard Transformer, allowing reuse of LLM infrastructure and methods, focusing on data curation and scaling.

The linked pages discuss the development and aims of MarinDNA, a 1B genomic language model that combines data curation, hyperparameter transfer, and scaling to achieve balanced performance across genomic tasks.
